[stale.9]
task = "8.4"
slice = "readme"
file = "README.md"
line = 126
severity = "missing"
stale = "- **Density.** `?density=agent`, the `x-rex-density` header, or a stored preference sets `data-rex-density=\"agent\"` on the document root, which removes animation and transition time, expands collapsed `<details>`, and gives controls a 44 by 44 CSS pixel minimum."
actual = "Per spec [decision] screen_fit and the code, the document root carries data-rex-screen (phone|tablet|desktop|wide), data-rex-pointer (coarse|fine) and data-rex-density (comfortable|compact|agent): packages/rex/src/client/screen.ts:24-27,33-50 (SCREEN_ATTRIBUTES, SCREEN_BREAKPOINTS, DEFAULT_SCREEN_DENSITY \"comfortable\"), packages/rex/src/client/agent/density.ts:36-42 DENSITY_PREFERENCES, server classification from Sec-CH-UA-Mobile/Sec-CH-Viewport-Width with a user-agent fallback (packages/rex/src/server/adapters/client-hints.ts; docs/agent-contract.md \"Screen\", lines 169-187); useScreen() exposes all three and the sidecar carries them. README has no Screen bullet and names only the agent density."
fix = "Open the Density bullet with: `?density=agent`, the `x-rex-density` header, or a stored preference (`localStorage` key `rex:density`) sets `data-rex-density=\"agent\"` on the document root (`comfortable` is the default and `compact` the third value), which removes animation and transition time, expands collapsed `<details>`, and gives controls a 44 by 44 CSS pixel minimum. Add after it: - **Screen.** The runtime classifies the screen (`phone`, `tablet`, `desktop`, `wide`), the pointer (`coarse`, `fine`) and the density (`comfortable`, `compact`, `agent`) and writes them on the document root as `data-rex-screen`, `data-rex-pointer` and `data-rex-density`: on the server (`screenFromRequest` in `packages/rex/src/server/ssr.ts`) from the `Sec-CH-UA-Mobile` and `Sec-CH-Viewport-Width` Client Hints (every HTML response sends `Accept-CH`) with a user-agent fallback, on the client from `matchMedia` and a `ResizeObserver`. `useScreen()` returns all three and the sidecar carries them. Overlays render as a dialog on tablet and larger screens and as a bottom sheet on phone; navigation is a dock on phone, a bar on tablet and a sidebar on desktop and wide screens."

