actual = "startNodeServer and createNodeApp live in packages/rex/src/server/adapters/node.ts (lines 44-104; node.ts re-exports them at line 25). createNodeApp sends GET/HEAD page paths (no extension) to the app first and returns its response when it carries the x-rex-render header (SSR or the static cache), otherwise serves static assets and then falls back to index.html with the Accept-CH/Vary client hints (lines 56-72). server/node.ts adds installNodeStaticPages, createPrerenderedNodeApp and startPrerenderedNodeServer (lines 69-104)."
fix = "On Node, `startNodeServer(app, { port, clientDir, hostname? })` (`packages/rex/src/server/adapters/node.ts`, re-exported by `server/node.ts`) wraps the app: a `GET` or `HEAD` request outside `/rex` for a path with a file extension is served from `clientDir`; a path without one goes to the app first and its response is returned when it carries `x-rex-render` (SSR, the csr shell or a prerendered page from the static cache), otherwise `clientDir` is tried and then `index.html` is sent with the client-hint headers; everything else goes to the app. `server/node.ts` adds `installNodeStaticPages` (reads the prerender list and registers the regenerating static cache), `createPrerenderedNodeApp` and `startPrerenderedNodeServer`, which `rex build`'s server entry uses."

